WEBVTT

00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:03.880
Before taking over a command workstation, check which application

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.349
and environment you are using.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.560
We begin in IC's Calls workspace, with the department's training

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.000
incidents already listed.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.439
Open the menu at the upper left and choose Settings.

00:00:14.899 --> 00:00:20.360
At the top, App Info shows App Name, Version and Environment; this example

00:00:20.389 --> 00:00:23.000
identifies Resgrid IC in development.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.620
That gives a command aide useful details when reporting a problem.

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:31.600
For practice, locate those three values, then find the Account section

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.409
directly underneath before reviewing connection or sign-in settings.

00:00:35.549 --> 00:00:40.059
In Settings, Account, open Server to inspect the connection address.

00:00:40.489 --> 00:00:44.650
The form shows Custom and a complete Server URL; the loopback

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.610
address here belongs to this local training environment.

00:00:47.999 --> 00:00:51.440
Use the address supplied by your administrator for your own installation.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.860
The note says to leave off the API version path and a trailing slash.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.440
Cancel closes this review without saving a different server.

00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:03.560
During a command handover, comparing the address first helps avoid

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.520
troubleshooting the wrong installation.

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:08.700
Practice finding the complete address rather than relying

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.179
on the shortened Account row.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.320
Back in Account, choose Sign-in and security.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.399
Read each section as the current account's summary.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.040
Here, Authenticator app says it is not set up, and Passkeys for

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.799
this app says there are none yet.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.000
Responder approvals lists Macintosh with Approvals stopped.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.649
Recent verifications reports no verifications in the last thirty days.

00:01:32.059 --> 00:01:36.090
These are separate facts, so check each rather than treating one heading

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.760
as a general security verdict.

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:41.029
If your department requires another method, arrange its

00:01:41.029 --> 00:01:42.479
approved setup separately.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.619
This review does not enroll an authenticator or create a passkey.

00:01:46.859 --> 00:01:49.000
In Account, Login Info

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.850
opens the Username and Password form.

00:01:51.339 --> 00:01:54.600
Both fields are empty in this demonstration, and Cancel and

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.169
Save are visible together.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:01.589
Save submits these details to sign in; it is not an account password-change screen.

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:06.420
For a routine workstation review, leave the fields empty and choose Cancel.

00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:10.420
This is especially useful when a supervisor is showing a colleague where

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:14.990
account access lives: you can explain the form without putting anyone's credentials

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:17.199
into a shared presentation or recording.

00:02:17.419 --> 00:02:21.129
In Account, Shared device is the place to review a workstation

00:02:21.129 --> 00:02:22.740
used by several operators.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.250
The page explains the shared-session purpose, shows This is a shared

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.210
device switched on, and offers a Device label, which is optional.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:34.739
The important note says this takes effect the next time

00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:36.519
someone signs in on this device.

00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:40.839
The form shown here has not been saved, so its switch alone does not

00:02:40.839 --> 00:02:42.730
prove a shared policy is active.

00:02:43.089 --> 00:02:46.000
Before a shift handover, compare this choice with

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.530
department guidance and decide who should configure it.

00:02:48.749 --> 00:02:53.219
Lower in Settings, Preferences groups the display and device choices.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:57.749
Theme currently shows System, while Language shows Select option.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.409
Keep Alive is off, and BT Handset says No device selected.

00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:06.269
Check these displayed states before assuming a workstation has your

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:09.859
preferred presentation or audio arrangement; this browser view

00:03:09.859 --> 00:03:13.709
does not demonstrate a connected handset or a device staying awake.

00:03:14.219 --> 00:03:19.660
Immediately below, Support lists Help Center, Contact Us, System Status,

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.109
Privacy Policy and Terms of Service.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.839
For practice, identify the appropriate support destination without opening

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.639
an external page during this review.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:33.530
In Settings, Sync and Offline Queue shows a Sync Status of Up to date.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.599
Choose View Sync Queue for the detailed picture.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:41.619
This session is Online, with zero pending, zero failed and zero done,

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.060
and the center says Queue is empty.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.509
The queue actions are disabled because there is nothing here to process or clear.

00:03:48.929 --> 00:03:52.959
An empty queue is a useful handover check, but it does not demonstrate an

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.039
offline write or successful replay.

00:03:55.439 --> 00:03:58.650
Practice reading connectivity and all three counts together

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.739
before describing the current sync state to another operator.

00:04:01.899 --> 00:04:05.000
Finally, in Account, choose Logout to

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.289
read Confirm Logout.

00:04:06.769 --> 00:04:11.279
The warning says logout will clear app data, cached values and settings.

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:15.819
Choose Cancel to finish this review while keeping the session; an actual

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:17.430
logout is a separate decision.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:22.169
The same checks help a fire or EMS command aide, a community crisis

00:04:22.169 --> 00:04:27.430
coordinator, a search-and-rescue lead, a security supervisor, a wildland command

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.969
team or an industrial response desk.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:34.170
In each setting, a useful handover names the environment, account

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:38.200
state and current queue rather than leaving the next operator to guess.

